Immediate Aftermath

Camera running along damaged scaffold.

Radio chatter fragments (distorted):
“Stabilize base three—”

Dust still falling from recent impact.

Satellite dishes scanning frantically.

The Moon surface shows a new crater.

Cause: Impact happened recently.

00:04–00:08

They Try to Fix It

Crew firing drilling rigs into fractured surface to anchor supports.

Vibration increases.

One drill penetrates deeper than expected.

Sudden harmonic tone.

Sub-bass tremor.

Cause → Drill breaches something metallic.

00:08–00:11

The First Sign

The drill stops.

Not jammed.

Stopped from below.

Surface crack spreads outward in a geometric line.

Dust falls into a seam.

The seam glows faintly.

Cause → They pierced an internal layer.

00:11–00:14

Revelation

Camera peers into the opening.

Beneath the crust:
Rotating internal rings.

Not rock.

Machined structure.

Ancient.

The “impact crater” edges reveal symmetry — too perfect.

Cause → Impact exposed internal mechanism.

00:14–00:17

Realization

Satellite dishes suddenly synchronize.

Not scanning.

Receiving.

All dishes tilt toward the Moon’s horizon simultaneously.

Signal tone rises.

Crew frozen.

Cause → The structure is responding to something.

00:17–00:20

Activation

Massive internal rings begin accelerating.

Gravity shifts.

Loose tools slide toward crater.

The colony tilts.

Low choir rises.

Cause → The drill acted as a trigger.

00:20–00:23

The Truth

Camera forced upward.

The “impact crater” on the Moon rotates.

It wasn’t damage.

It was a key.

The Moon rotates slightly — locking orientation.

Stars shift.

Cause → The impact aligned it.

00:23–00:25

Final Realization

Massive planetary-scale seams light up across lunar surface.

The impact site forms a perfect geometric node.

Radio whisper (cutting out):
“…it wasn’t an accident…”

Black.